# qwen3.5-2b-jetson — NVIDIA Jetson Orin (8 GB) tutor model, small tier
#
# Build:   ollama create qwen3.5-2b-jetson -f infra/ollama/Modelfile.qwen3.5-2b-jetson
# Use:     TUTOR_MODEL_OVERRIDE=local_ollama/qwen3.5-2b-jetson
#          or pick it in /admin/ (ModelConfig, purpose=tutoring)
#
# WHY A TAG AND NOT JUST THE PROFILE — this is the whole point of the file.
# apps/llm/model_profiles.py can only pin num_ctx on requests that go through
# our own Ollama client. The grader's Tier-2 verifier does NOT: it reaches
# Ollama through instructor.from_provider('ollama'), which uses the
# OPENAI-COMPATIBLE endpoint (POST /v1/chat/completions), and that endpoint has
# no field for num_ctx.
#
# Ollama keys a loaded runner on (model, params). So the verifier's call landed
# at Ollama's 4096 default, which is a DIFFERENT runner from the tutor's 16384 —
# and under OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=1 that evicts the tutor and reloads from
# scratch, 30-45 s each way. Measured on plain qwen3.5:2b (2026-07-28): the
# service log alternates 16384 / 4096 cells, two full reloads per graded turn.
#
# A Modelfile PARAMETER applies on EVERY endpoint, so pinning it here is the
# only fix that covers the paths we do not construct requests for. This is
# exactly why Modelfile.qwen3-4b-jetson never showed the problem.
FROM qwen3.5:2b

# Must match local_ollama/qwen3.5-2b-jetson in apps/llm/model_profiles.py.
# If the two disagree, the disagreement IS the bug — the tutor path sends the
# profile value while every other path inherits this one, and they thrash.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

# Qwen3.5's own recommended sampling (framework §3.3), restated here so the tag
# is self-describing and the OpenAI-compatible path gets them too.
PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
